WEBVTT

NOTE Narration by an AI voice: Matilda (XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX), eleven_v4.

intro
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:07.020
Here, Cursor CLI repairs a saved search that stopped working on a real Splunk Cloud stack.

health
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.960
A quick splunkctl check first. The stack is green.

ask
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:21.400
The prompt asks Cursor to fix a failing saved search without editing the search itself.

run
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.800
Cursor runs the failing search first, to get the real error.

parser
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:36.140
The parser error says the search calls a macro that Splunk can't find.

context
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:44.060
It checks the saved search and a sample of the checkout logs, so the fix matches the actual data.

count
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:54.020
Then it counts 5xx errors by region on the real checkout data, to confirm what the search should return.

why-stop
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.800
Splunkctl holds this change for approval.

deploy
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:06.900
Approved. Cursor runs the same command once, and the macro is created.

rerun
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.140
Next, it reruns the saved search to prove the fix works.

results
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.940
All four regions return errors again.

outro
00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.500
A final check confirms the macro is live, and the search works again.
